  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 151 AM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nWildfire smoke today is likely to be very similar to how it was \nyesterday. Meaning it will still be noticeable in the air and still \nmake air quality \"moderate\" to \"unhealthy for sensitive groups,\" but \nnot impact visibility or be as thick as it was earlier in the week. \nThat said, air quality alerts still continue for parts of the \neastern Magic Valley today. The heat up is on and highs today are \nlooking to warm into the mid to upper 90s for most of the Snake \nRiver Plain and lower elevations in the South Hills and Central \nMountains. Otherwise, look for more mid to upper 80s in our mid-\nelevation towns. Wind gusts this afternoon once again will be around \n20 to 25 mph for many. Expect Friday, Saturday, and Sunday to be \nalmost identical weather days with highs back in the 90s to low \ntriple digits. Overnight temperatures will also be warmer, likely \nstaying in the upper 50s and low to mid 60s for many, so heat \nproducts may need to be issued later today, especially for parts of \nthe eastern Magic Valley and South Hills. Early next week, troughing \nbegins to move into the West, which will help flatten our ridge of \nhigh pressure and slowly push it a bit farther east, allowing \nmonsoon moisture to make its way back into East Idaho. Which, at \nthis point, we will welcome any potential precipitation chances. \nThis slight pattern change brings a slight drop in our afternoon \ntemperatures, but they will likely still remain in the low to mid \n90s for the second half of next week.",
